e <span class = \"italic\">Go  straight ahead, Turn right</span> or <span class = \"italic\">Turn left</span>. You do not use a subject.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":\"2\",\"columns\":\"2\",\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Asking for directions\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Giving directions\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Where is ... ?<br/>Where do I find ... ?<br/>How do I get to ... ?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Go straight ahead.<br/>Turn right/left.<br/>Walk across the bridge.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "<span class = \"strong\">Andrew</span>: Excuse me, how do I get to the stadium?<br/><span class = \"strong\">Beth</span>: Go straight ahead.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class = \"strong\">Michael</span>: Where is the library?<br/><span class = \"strong\">Patrick</span>: It's right here. Go straight and turn left.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Things to Do in the City", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " There are many things you can do in a city. Read the chart below for a list of free time activities:", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":\"3\",\"columns\":\"3\",\"cells\":[\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Inside\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Outside\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Place: <span class = \\\"italic\\\">I go to the ...</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"bakery<br/>restaurant<br/>swimming pool\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"stadium<br/>park<br/>square\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Activity: <span class = \\\"italic\\\">I like to ...</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"eat<br/>swim\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"run<br/>walk\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "<span class = \"strong\">Peter</span>: What is there to do in the neighborhood?<br/><span class = \"strong\">Vanessa</span>: There are many restaurants near the park. We can walk to the park and then eat in a restaurant!", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "behind", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to the back of something or someone", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(preposition)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The bakery is on the street behind the swimming pool.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le06ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to ask for directions.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "bridge", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a structure that carries a road over water", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Turn left and walk across the bridge.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le06ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "I'm not sure", "type": "name"}, {"content": "I don't know", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: <span class = \"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Where is the bakery?  <span class = \"strong\">Peter</span>: I'm not sure.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le06ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "in front of", "type": "name"}, {"content": "ahead of something or someone", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(preposition)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Let's ask the person in front of the store.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le06ob02aud04", "type": "audio"